This just means that your initial stack of regular daggers will
grow quickly to the point you can start ditching the orcish
ones.  Then you can gradually build your stacks of elvish ones
until you have slowly replaced the regular ones.

You don't need to carry exactly one stack of daggers.  The
"t"hrow function works with any item at all.  And early on when
you still have all sorts of daggers that have not yet stacked,
you haven't yet built up the skill to machine-gun they several
at a time anyways.

It adds up great - During the time the game allows you to
throw one dagger at a time, the game starts to supply you with
an assortment of daggers were some stack and some don't.
By the time your skills allow throwing several at once the
game has supplied you with enough daggers that you have
stacks not individual ones.



